"""v15 Error-Driven Recovery Playbook.

v14 only fed the playbook from "click had no visible effect"; real failure codes (`[OCCLUDED]`, `[SECURITY_DENIED]`, `CDP closed`) were handed
back to the LLM, which then burned steps re-trying the same thing (run log: task #2 -> maxsteps, playbook count 0).

v15 closes the loop INSIDE the action step (the model never sees a recovered failure, so no decision step is consumed):

  [OCCLUDED]         -> identify the blocker from the evidence (`covered by hwnd N`) -> popup/menu: Esc | shell/own console: raise the target
                        (verified focus_window) | other window: minimize it -> re-run the SAME action in place (max 2 rounds)
  [SECURITY_DENIED]  -> put the tool/command signature on the task's DENY LIST, inject a concrete safe alternative into the next prompt,
                        pre-block identical re-tries; the 2nd identical denial switches the state machine to SAFE_TERMINATE
                        (status `blocked_security`, evidence attached) instead of grinding to maxsteps
  CDP closed/crashed -> hub.cdp_heal() (500 ms back-off reconnect, browser relaunch with the same profile) -> re-run the action

All activity is appended to `events` (the trace archived by evals/ as the "error recovery trajectory").
